-- title:
--   Reduced diamond action commutes with extension of constants
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $K$ be algebraically closed fields with $K$ a $k$-algebra, let $N \geq 1$ be an integer with $(N : k) \neq 0$, and let $H' \leq (\mathbb{Z}/N)^{\times}$ be a subgroup. Write $\Gamma_{H'} =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H'`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image under the inclusion $\Gamma_0(N) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H'$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^{\times}$ sending $\gamma$ to the class of its lower-right entry, and for a field $L$ let $F_L =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC L Γ_{H'}`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the ratios $\overline{p_f}/\overline{p_g}$, where $f, g$ are modular forms of a common weight for $\Gamma_{H'}$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ and the image of $p_g$ in $L((q))$ is nonzero. Let $\iota\colon F_k \to F_K$ be a ring homomorphism which on underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) applied to $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,k\,K$, i.e. coefficientwise application of $k \to K$. Then for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ and every $x \in F_k$, $\iota(\rho_k(\gamma)\,x) = \rho_K(\gamma)(\iota\,x)$, where $\rho_L =$ [`ModularCurve.diamondActionModL L N H'`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L203) is the monoid homomorphism from $\Gamma_0(N)$ to $\mathrm{Aut}_L(F_L)$ chosen (when one exists, otherwise trivial) so as to satisfy [`ModularCurve.IsDiamondPullbackModL`](def/ModularCurve_XHDiamondModL.html#L12): whenever $f_1 = f\mid_k\gamma$ and $g_1 = g\mid_k\gamma$ for forms with integral expansions $p_f, p_g, p_{f_1}, p_{g_1}$ and $\overline{p_g} \neq 0$, the element with series $\overline{p_{f_1}}/\overline{p_{g_1}}$ is sent to the element with series $\overline{p_f}/\overline{p_g}$.
--
--   The statement expresses that the reduced diamond operators on the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H'}(N)$ are insensitive to enlarging the algebraically closed field of constants, the characterising pull-back property being formulated through $q$-expansions with integral coefficients. It is used in the comparison of the diamond action with Frobenius places on the $q$-expansion function field, in [`ModularCurve.diamondActionModL_smul_mem_ssPlacesQExp_iff_and_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.diamondActionModL_smul_mem_ssPlacesQExp_iff_and_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_eq_smul).
